From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JetBox build <build@jetbox.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:15:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] jetbox: make system-visible names build-time variables

New package client/jetboxbrand holds the names the service leaves in the
system or shares with an official NetBird installed on the same computer:
service name/display name/description, Windows firewall rule, NRPT key
prefix, macOS scutil key prefix, data directories (state default, panic
log, tmp-install), UPnP mapping description, the legacy config directory
copied on first start, CLI defaults (daemon address, log and run dirs),
MDM policy location (macOS plist, Windows registry), the ssh_config.d file
and the launchd logs collected by the debug bundle.

Defaults equal upstream; JetBox builds set them with -ldflags -X.
